WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.664 --> 00:00:07.589
A man: Hayya Alal Salat. Hayya Alal Salat.

2
00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:14.580
Hayya Alal Falah. Hayya Alal Falah.

3
00:00:15.689 --> 00:00:20.675
Allahu Akbar. Allahu Akbar.

4
00:00:21.699 --> 00:00:27.154
A man: La Elaha Ella Allah.

5
00:00:33.327 --> 00:00:34.743
Dean Majul: Alhamdu Lillah,

6
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.260
Alhamdu Lillahi Lazzi Hadana Bil Iman Wa Al-Islam.

7
00:00:39.473 --> 00:00:42.710
Ash-hadu Alla Elaha Ella Allah Wahdahu La Shareeka Lah.

8
00:00:42.923 --> 00:00:44.923
Wa Ashhadu Anna Muhammadan Abduhu Wa Rasuluh
(This was later removed from the Shahaadah)

9
00:00:45.776 --> 00:00:51.232
(3:102) ٱتَّقُوا ٱللَّهَ حَقَّ تُقَاتِهِ وَلَا تَمُوتُنَّ إِلَّا وَأَنتُم مُّسْلِمُونَ

10
00:00:52.512 --> 00:00:59.555
I'm afraid that this Khutba is going to, to be, it would be longer than you thought.

11
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:09.123
I'll try to be very fast. So, I beg of you, your attention and concentration. And I have to go very fast.

12
00:01:10.445 --> 00:01:22.000
The Khutba, at least the first part, will deal with the methodology or technique in understanding better or understanding the Quran,

13
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.550
or how to get more out of the Quran.

14
00:01:26.341 --> 00:01:34.293
The second Khutba will be dedicated to just one example to illustrate the pointers in the first Khutba.

15
00:01:36.085 --> 00:01:40.744
And let me just remind you about three quotations from the Quran.

16
00:01:41.341 --> 00:01:46.403
You know this very well. Ustaz (teacher) has repeated and re-repeated it.

17
00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:48.677
So, let me repeat it again.

18
00:01:50.597 --> 00:01:51.758
First,

19
00:01:51.758 --> 00:01:56.104
[6:38]  ... We did not leave anything out of this scripture.** ...

20
00:01:56.104 --> 00:01:56.952
or book.

21
00:01:58.062 --> 00:01:59.545
Sura 6:38.

22
00:02:01.545 --> 00:02:02.607
Remember that, no?

23
00:02:02.607 --> 00:02:03.895
Second,

24
00:02:03.895 --> 00:02:11.185
[6:114]  Shall I seek other than GOD as a source of law, when He revealed to you this book fully detailed?* ...

25
00:02:12.555 --> 00:02:13.455
[6:115]  The word ...

26
00:02:13.455 --> 00:02:14.692
(unintelligible)

27
00:02:14.692 --> 00:02:18.825
[6:115]  The word of your Lord is complete,* in truth and justice. ...

28
00:02:19.209 --> 00:02:20.806
Sura 6:115.

29
00:02:20.806 --> 00:02:22.555
14 and 15.

30
00:02:22.555 --> 00:02:25.000
The third one,

31
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:31.360
After saying that (unintelligible) and Allah had put the Quran together, after reciting it, we say it.

32
00:02:31.573 --> 00:02:34.573
Then, it is we who will explain it.

33
00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:35.976
I think it's very clear.

34
00:02:36.573 --> 00:02:39.573
Allah says He has not left anything out of this scripture.

35
00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:45.000
It is complete, perfect, detailed, and He will explain it.

36
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:49.000
After He revealed or after the recitation.

37
00:02:50.962 --> 00:02:55.133
These quotations clearly imply that the questions raised by the Quran,...

38
00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:58.427
see, the Quran raises questions,

39
00:02:58.427 --> 00:03:03.597
or questions raised by Muslims,

40
00:03:03.597 --> 00:03:08.000
where the answers of these will be found in the Quran itself.

41
00:03:08.683 --> 00:03:09.489
All right?

42
00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:16.242
If we take these quotations the way Allah presents it to us, it means, if the Quran raises a question,

43
00:03:16.242 --> 00:03:21.000
or if we raise a question, the answer must be found in the Quran.

44
00:03:22.322 --> 00:03:24.128
I hope you agree with me on that point.

45
00:03:24.554 --> 00:03:27.085
If not, then just listen to what I have to say.

46
00:03:30.555 --> 00:03:36.915
Now, we must not talk in the Quran for irrelevant or insignificant things.

47
00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:47.000
Let us not go to Quran to find a recipe for chicken curry or Afghan pilaf, for example.

48
00:03:47.725 --> 00:03:52.090
But, certainly, if you know the Quran enough,

49
00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:58.000
the Quran tells us, do not serve poisoned curry to your friends or to your enemies. (unintelligible)

50
00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.000
On the contrary, if you're cooking curry and you have a hungry guest,

51
00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.123
you serve him, you feed him, feed the hungry.

52
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:12.000
The Quran, in many instances, says that men of understanding know

53
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.550
or will come to know the revelations of Allah.

54
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:20.469
So, it seems that there is another way of knowing the Quran,

55
00:04:20.469 --> 00:04:22.000
if you have understanding.

56
00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:25.000
But this is apparent, because when we ask the question,

57
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.000
who are men of understanding?

58
00:04:27.384 --> 00:04:28.384
They are the righteous.

59
00:04:28.384 --> 00:04:30.000
Then, who are the righteous?

60
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.000
They are the believers and they are those who study the Quran.

61
00:04:33.469 --> 00:04:40.171
So, either Allah explains it to you directly and you will know the answer,

62
00:04:40.171 --> 00:04:44.427
or you have understanding, but the man of understanding is one who goes to Quran.

63
00:04:44.427 --> 00:04:48.000
So, in any case, the answer is indeed Quran.

64
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.171
I hope this is a,

65
00:04:49.171 --> 00:04:51.000
this is a logical technique.

66
00:04:51.213 --> 00:04:55.000
If A gives you B, and not A gives you B,

67
00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.787
since either A or not A in any case, it is B.

68
00:04:57.787 --> 00:05:00.000
So, it's the Quran in any case.

69
00:05:00.573 --> 00:05:03.787
Whether Allah tells it to you directly or you use your understanding,

70
00:05:03.787 --> 00:05:05.806
it's still to the Quran.

71
00:05:07.299 --> 00:05:13.299
Yet, there are dangers or obstacles or warnings,

72
00:05:13.299 --> 00:05:18.280
which I think we should mention in trying to get explanations to our questions,

73
00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:23.104
or to get further elucidation to Quranic verses.

74
00:05:24.213 --> 00:05:25.360
The first warning.

75
00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.573
So, this is just my opinion.

76
00:05:27.573 --> 00:05:29.421
It's up to you to let people know.

77
00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:40.934
First is too much emphasis on the Jewish Bible in making us understand the Quran.

78
00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.763
I said too much emphasis.

79
00:05:46.024 --> 00:05:48.958
The Bible, the Jewish Bible in particular,

80
00:05:48.958 --> 00:05:53.617
has been edited, re-edited, and re-re-edited,

81
00:05:53.617 --> 00:05:58.829
and it has assumed its final form only 150 years before Christ,

82
00:05:58.829 --> 00:06:01.829
after the Babylonian captivity.

83
00:06:02.597 --> 00:06:09.042
That is after Ezra edited it, prescribes, re-edited it.

84
00:06:09.597 --> 00:06:14.000
Now this is accepted by biblical scholars.

85
00:06:15.512 --> 00:06:21.512
And Muslims must not have an inferiority complex

86
00:06:21.512 --> 00:06:25.294
by depending so much on the Jewish scriptures.

87
00:06:27.597 --> 00:06:30.597
Or, the other way around,

88
00:06:30.597 --> 00:06:36.000
Muslims should not be so proud that they know so much about the Jewish Bible.

89
00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:41.469
Because you will find out, if you read these Tafsirs (interpretations) of our ancestors,

90
00:06:41.469 --> 00:06:45.024
anything that is difficult in the Quran to them,

91
00:06:45.024 --> 00:06:46.787
they quote the Bible,

92
00:06:46.787 --> 00:06:50.000
not so much to help us understand the Quran,

93
00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:53.445
but to show that they know so much about the Jewish Bible.

94
00:06:53.445 --> 00:06:57.701
And in trying to show so much that they know about the Jewish Bible,

95
00:06:57.701 --> 00:06:59.701
they begin to forget their own Quran.

96
00:06:59.701 --> 00:07:02.189
Now, this happens to reverent Muslims.

97
00:07:03.341 --> 00:07:08.317
It is a defect which many of us have, including your humble self.

98
00:07:08.829 --> 00:07:10.232
It's showing off. I noticed that.

99
00:07:10.232 --> 00:07:11.616
I fall into the trap.

100
00:07:11.616 --> 00:07:13.403
I always want to show that I know the Bible,

101
00:07:13.403 --> 00:07:16.611
at least, to show that I didn't waste 12 years in a Catholic school.

102
00:07:18.787 --> 00:07:21.470
Now, we have to be, we have to check ourselves,

103
00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:24.213
check our pride that we know something about the Bible,

104
00:07:24.213 --> 00:07:28.659
and at the same time, not to have this inferiority complex.

105
00:07:28.659 --> 00:07:31.427
Because in the first hundred years of Islam,

106
00:07:31.427 --> 00:07:35.000
when there were discussions with Christians in Syria and so on,

107
00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:38.787
the Muslims had to show that they also knew what the Christians knew.

108
00:07:38.787 --> 00:07:40.635
But this is historical.

109
00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:47.659
We must also consider that the Jewish Bible serves national purposes,

110
00:07:47.659 --> 00:07:50.000
genealogical purposes.

111
00:07:50.829 --> 00:07:53.829
And that's the meaning of the editing.

112
00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:58.531
It's always to show that the Jews are a distinct people, different from others.

113
00:07:58.531 --> 00:08:02.256
And this overemphasis that they are the chosen people

114
00:08:02.256 --> 00:08:08.592
makes them, in their editing, emphasize more what is to their direct interest.

115
00:08:09.488 --> 00:08:22.341
Also, it's not at all safe to always explain the Quran through the Bible as we now have it.

116
00:08:22.341 --> 00:08:25.171
But there is a qualification.

117
00:08:25.171 --> 00:08:29.573
There is nothing wrong in pointing out certain correspondences

118
00:08:29.573 --> 00:08:37.213
between events or incidents or characters in the Quran and those in the Bible.

119
00:08:37.213 --> 00:08:39.299
This is not just a matter of (unintelligible),

120
00:08:39.299 --> 00:08:42.488
but it is a matter of developing our understanding.

121
00:08:43.171 --> 00:08:46.342
Please do not misunderstand me, brothers and sisters,

122
00:08:46.342 --> 00:08:48.299
or sisters and brothers occasionally.

123
00:08:48.299 --> 00:08:49.763
I don't know what's the protocol.

124
00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:54.384
I'm not saying we should not consult the Jewish Bible.

125
00:08:54.384 --> 00:08:56.470
I say let us not overemphasise.

126
00:08:56.470 --> 00:09:00.242
On the contrary, it is good to show certain correspondences

127
00:09:00.242 --> 00:09:05.224
if, in the final analysis, it will help us understand the Quran.

128
00:09:06.485 --> 00:09:08.485
As long as events are consistent,

129
00:09:08.485 --> 00:09:10.000
well and good.

130
00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:12.000
But when there are discrepancies,

131
00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:15.000
then the Quran must be the final one.

132
00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:18.079
It must supersede the Bible.

133
00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:24.000
Other things in the Bible can be dismissed as irrelevant to the Quranic message,

134
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.000
details about rituals, details about sacrifices,

135
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:31.000
the lives of their kings, their adulteries, their incest,

136
00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.625
all of these things, this is all irrelevant.

137
00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:39.115
The great danger is to interpret, or understand the Quran

138
00:09:39.115 --> 00:09:43.000
solely, exclusively in terms of the Bible,

139
00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:47.000
rather than letting the Quran explain itself,

140
00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:52.000
or letting Allah explain Himself in the Quran.

141
00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:55.000
This, however, does not mean, as I said,

142
00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:57.242
that we must neglect the Bible entirely.

143
00:09:57.242 --> 00:10:00.000
On the contrary, as I will try to show,

144
00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.000
it will be of some help in giving additional information.

145
00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:07.551
But, as I will try to show, it is an information

146
00:10:07.551 --> 00:10:11.000
that can be reached back by the Quran,

147
00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:14.242
and must be totally, be consistent with the Quran.

148
00:10:14.242 --> 00:10:16.000
Needless to say,

149
00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:20.921
just (unintelligible) is consulting the Hadith

150
00:10:20.921 --> 00:10:22.000
to explain the Quran.

151
00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:24.224
This is superfluous, huh?

152
00:10:25.388 --> 00:10:29.146
There are people who use the Hadith to explain Quran.

153
00:10:29.146 --> 00:10:30.758
I would like to give you examples of this,

154
00:10:30.758 --> 00:10:32.758
because some of them are very,

155
00:10:32.758 --> 00:10:34.758
I mean, are very comical, I would say.

156
00:10:34.758 --> 00:10:37.370
In any case, this must be avoided.

157
00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:42.000
A criteria to guide us is that the Quran is flawless,

158
00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.418
totally consistent,

159
00:10:43.418 --> 00:10:46.321
as stated in the Sura 18, verse 1.

160
00:10:47.339 --> 00:10:49.757
Quran also talks about Masallans,

161
00:10:49.757 --> 00:10:52.418
examples, speaks of allegories,

162
00:10:52.418 --> 00:10:54.709
similitudes, analogies, etc.,

163
00:10:54.709 --> 00:10:56.740
together with direct verses.

164
00:10:57.709 --> 00:11:00.291
And, let me quote,

165
00:11:00.291 --> 00:11:01.291
(unintelligible) of Allah,

166
00:11:01.291 --> 00:11:14.110
[3:7]  He is the one who revealed this scripture to you, with perfect verses that must be taken literally—as constituting the essence of the scripture. Other verses are allegorical. ...

167
00:11:15.469 --> 00:11:16.805
(3:7) مُتَشَٰبِهَٰتٌ

168
00:11:17.914 --> 00:11:34.546
[3:7]  ... Those who harbor doubts in their hearts dwell on the allegorical verses to create confusion, and misrepresentation thereof. No one knows the correct interpretation thereof except GOD and those well founded in knowledge. ...

169
00:11:34.546 --> 00:11:36.546
Those who listen to Allah.

170
00:11:36.787 --> 00:11:37.849
(unintelligible)

171
00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:43.000
And, it's very clear,

172
00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:47.000
some people avoid the clear verses of the Quran,

173
00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:48.000
or rather,

174
00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:51.000
they concentrate on the allegories

175
00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:54.000
to forget the clear verses of the Quran

176
00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:57.000
in order to bring dissension and so on.

177
00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.384
But Allah does not tell us

178
00:11:58.384 --> 00:12:02.000
that we should not try to study these allegories.

179
00:12:02.469 --> 00:12:05.469
We should try to understand these allegories of the Quran,

180
00:12:05.469 --> 00:12:08.000
but not use them to create dissension.

181
00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:12.303
One of the ideas here of these verses is that such allegories

182
00:12:12.303 --> 00:12:14.213
must not be interpreted

183
00:12:14.213 --> 00:12:16.213
in an arbitrary manner

184
00:12:16.213 --> 00:12:18.299
so as to cause dissension

185
00:12:18.299 --> 00:12:21.701
for religious or sectarian motives.

186
00:12:22.085 --> 00:12:23.597
Their interpretation

187
00:12:23.597 --> 00:12:26.384
must be in terms of the Quranic verses

188
00:12:26.384 --> 00:12:30.640
in a consistent or logical manner.

189
00:12:31.024 --> 00:12:32.384
Allah says,

190
00:12:32.384 --> 00:12:45.000
[11:1]  A. L. R. ... a scripture whose verses were perfectly designed, then elucidated.* ... from the One who is Wise, Cognizant.

191
00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:46.000
In brief,

192
00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:48.384
Allah Himself declares

193
00:12:48.384 --> 00:12:50.000
that He explains

194
00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:53.000
or elucidates His allegories.

195
00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:54.903
In the second Khutba,

196
00:12:54.903 --> 00:12:56.469
we will have one example

197
00:12:56.469 --> 00:12:58.299
to explain all of these things

198
00:12:58.299 --> 00:12:59.640
that we have mentioned

199
00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:02.133
along theoretical lines.

200
00:13:03.541 --> 00:13:05.541
Astaghfirullah...

201
00:13:10.427 --> 00:13:12.787
Now, this is one example

202
00:13:12.787 --> 00:13:15.787
for your elucidation

203
00:13:15.787 --> 00:13:17.000
or not elucidation,

204
00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:19.213
for your edification. 

205
00:13:19.213 --> 00:13:20.507
and entertainment.

206
00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:25.000
One subject only, to illustrate what we have discussed.

207
00:13:25.256 --> 00:13:30.000
The problem of the nakedness of Adam and Eve. Ok?

208
00:13:32.654 --> 00:13:33.995
All of us,

209
00:13:33.995 --> 00:13:36.848
especially we who live in the western world,

210
00:13:36.848 --> 00:13:38.232
are inheritors

211
00:13:38.232 --> 00:13:39.360
or victims

212
00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:40.915
of western culture,

213
00:13:40.915 --> 00:13:42.512
or western paintings,

214
00:13:42.512 --> 00:13:44.067
or western movies,

215
00:13:44.067 --> 00:13:45.408
TVs and so on.

216
00:13:45.787 --> 00:13:47.000
What do we always see?

217
00:13:47.671 --> 00:13:50.780
We always see Adam and Eve

218
00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:52.573
depicted as

219
00:13:52.573 --> 00:13:54.379
physically naked.

220
00:13:55.019 --> 00:13:57.574
Even before the so-called (unintelligible)

221
00:13:59.171 --> 00:14:05.958
There's a movie, I saw a movie, that is (unintelligible). A young boy, a young girl, running.

222
00:14:05.958 --> 00:14:12.038
Well, there are (unintelligible) around, because they are naked. Then, you see Michelangelo's painting.

223
00:14:14.256 --> 00:14:18.673
Happy, a happy couple, young man and a young woman, naked.

224
00:14:22.256 --> 00:14:24.080
So, that is now in our mind.

225
00:14:26.511 --> 00:14:30.000
Now, Paradise was a kind of a new discovery.

226
00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:32.000
Ok.

227
00:14:35.171 --> 00:14:45.915
And from this, as well as our reading of the Bible, we begin to accept the second element,

228
00:14:45.915 --> 00:14:52.597
is that because of this nakedness, they use fig leaves. Ok?

229
00:14:53.536 --> 00:14:56.445
I don't know why fig leaves. I have an answer for that.

230
00:14:57.171 --> 00:15:01.171
But a little bit off-color, so I will not say.

231
00:15:01.171 --> 00:15:06.573
But if you look at the shape of the fig leaves, it's good enough to cover three aspects of a man's body.

232
00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:08.559
Okay.

233
00:15:10.559 --> 00:15:14.351
The Bible specifically mentions fig leaves.

234
00:15:14.872 --> 00:15:20.829
The Quran does not, huh? The Quran does not say that Adam and Eve

235
00:15:20.829 --> 00:15:22.938
covered themselves with fig leaves.

236
00:15:22.938 --> 00:15:28.000
The Quran only says, they covered themselves with leaves of the garden.

237
00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:30.208
More versatile.

238
00:15:32.597 --> 00:15:40.555
Now, the Bible says that after the fall, when they covered themselves with fig leaves,

239
00:15:40.555 --> 00:15:45.000
the good Lord taught them how to use skins.

240
00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:49.720
Very interesting. So, Allah, in the Jewish Bible, becomes a tailor.

241
00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:55.360
He tells Adam and Eve, no, fig leaves not good enough, skins.

242
00:15:55.573 --> 00:15:58.099
Maybe, the garden was becoming colder.

243
00:16:00.701 --> 00:16:05.336
What does the Quran say? Okay, let's go slowly and carefully.

244
00:16:06.659 --> 00:16:10.337
Sura 20, verses 117, 118.

